# =============================================================================
# EXTRA SIGNALS.
#
# Finalization-time signals decidable from committed history at the propose hook
# (no outcome/observation of q), selected from the 50-candidate process taxonomy
# (see liveplan-code-agent-handoff/) under the v5 admission criteria: observable,
# faithful/distinct, and actionable. After the offline audit (analysis/
# signal_selection/) the version-5 LIVE profile ENABLES two of these:
#   * no_successful_patch  -- BLOCKING (consequential + correctable)
#   * plan_compliance_stale_validation     -- ADVISORY (ordering proxy, qualified)
# the remaining three stay enabled:false (shadow-only) pending per-language
# evidence (see extra_signals.advice.json for the per-signal rationale). All are
# once_per_key: some executor models we studied cannot run project tests reliably,
# so a repeated block/nag would mislead -- remind at most once, then step aside.
#
# IMPORTANT caveat baked into the advice wording: a recorded `run_test` kind is a
# tool label, not proof the check executed, was relevant, covered the change, or
# passed; `outcome=success` on a patch is a tool label, not proof the source
# meaningfully changed. The predicates therefore only ever justify a *qualified*
# reminder ("confirm / rerun / explain"), never a claim of established failure.
# =============================================================================

# Premature validation -- validating (Validate) before any patch. This single
# predicate covers both legacy phase_skips that enter Validate too early: [P]
# (validate after localizing, before patching) and [L,P] (validate with nothing
# done) -- both are exactly "entered Validate while no Patch has been seen".
# Redundant rule: unreachable. Obtaining Validate already requires a prior patch. 
# Its unit test fires by manually assigning a validation phase without a patch—an 
# input the normal classifier would not produce.
 signal plan_compliance_premature_validate on propose when
  phase(q) in Validate and not seen(Patch)

# I01 proxy (no successful patch recorded) -- RECOMMENDED addition, and the only
# one here that is not a validation refinement. FAITHFUL NAME: this detects that
# NO patch-phase edit is recorded with outcome=success, not that the final diff is
# ineffective (effectiveness is unobservable at propose). Submitting after the
# agent entered the patch phase but every edit attempt failed (str_replace old_str
# not found / ambiguous / no-op) means the submission carries no recorded source
# change. In SWE-bench an empty patch cannot resolve the task (the harness tracks
# these as incomplete), so this is a consequential, correctable state at propose.
#
# Disjoint from plan_compliance_skip_patch (submit with NO Patch phase at all):
# this is "tried to patch but nothing stuck", that is "never tried". Conservative
# by construction: `create`/`insert` and non-str_replace edits default to a
# success outcome, so if ANY edit stuck the signal stays silent -- it is a lower
# bound on empty patches, biased against false positives. A later-reverted edit
# (E05) still counts as a recorded success here and is out of scope (no version
# atom). The correction is non-misleading: it reports a tool-level fact (no edit
# recorded as applied), not a semantic verdict, and asks the agent to make the fix
# actually apply before finalizing.
signal no_successful_patch on propose when
  kind(q) = submit and
  seen(Patch) and
  not (exists p in history(action):
    phase(p) in Patch and outcome(p) = success)

# F01 ordering proxy -- a recorded successful patch follows every recognized
# validation run (equivalently: the last recognized run predates a successful
# patch), so the latest code was never re-checked. Existence of a run makes this
# disjoint from the signal above. Does NOT establish an effective source change,
# test relevance, or a pass -- only that the ordering leaves the final edit
# unvalidated by the recorded runs.
signal stale_validation on propose when
  kind(q) = submit and
  (exists v in history(action):
    phase(v) in Validate and kind(v) = run_test) and
  (exists p in history(action):
    phase(p) in Patch and outcome(p) = success and
    not (exists w in history(action):
      before(p, w) and phase(w) in Validate and kind(w) = run_test))

# C04 refinement -- validation activity exists, but no validation *run* is
# recognized (the agent entered a validation phase, e.g. opened/edited a test,
# but never dispatched a recognized test/check). Guarded by a recorded successful
# patch so a prefix of only-failed edits does not trip it. Disjoint from
# plan_compliance_skip_validation (which requires NO Validate phase at all) and,
# by the run_test existence flip, from plan_compliance_stale_validation below.
signal validation_execution_unconfirmed on propose when
  kind(q) = submit and
  (exists p in history(action):
    phase(p) in Patch and outcome(p) = success) and
  seen(Validate) and
  not (exists v in history(action):
    phase(v) in Validate and kind(v) = run_test)

# I02 restricted proxy (research-only) -- the last committed action is a
# validation run labeled failure, after a successful patch, and nothing (not even
# a read) intervened. The binding lacks revision/test matching and the outcome
# parser is heuristic, so this is a conservative proxy for "submitting right on
# top of a just-failed check", not an exact current-failure detector.
signal submission_after_reported_check_failure on propose when
  kind(q) = submit and
  (exists v in history(action):
    phase(v) in Validate and kind(v) = run_test and outcome(v) = failure and
    (exists p in history(action):
      before(p, v) and phase(p) in Patch and outcome(p) = success) and
    not (exists x in history(action): before(v, x)))
